{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>I know</b> — then I will know." "<b>And the word יעשה</b> — on account of another [verse]: 'He will execute justice for the needy.'"], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 140, :notes {0 "The comment addresses a tense/form issue: the psalm's ידעתי (past/perfect form) is read as future, hence 'then I will know.'"}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:42:22.919681268Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}